infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Same result rows: HAVING-only 9 s vs WHERE-pushdown 0.2 s
  desc 12M-row orders, only 1.2M are paid — where the filter runs decides the cost
  compares
    - label HAVING only — group first, then drop groups
      children
        - label Seq Scan: 12,000,000 rows
          desc Every order reaches the grouping step — no row filter ran first
        - label 2,000,000 buckets built
          desc HashAggregate materializes a bucket for every user
        - label Spills 180 MB to disk -> 9 s
          desc Groups overflow work_mem, so the aggregate spills
    - label WHERE pushdown — filter first, then group
      children
        - label Bitmap Index Scan: 1,200,000 rows
          desc Partial index on status='paid' prunes 10x the input
        - label 400,000 buckets built
          desc Only surviving-user groups — 5x fewer to materialize
        - label Fits work_mem -> 0.2 s
          desc No disk spill; same result rows, 45x faster
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
